---
description: Dead-code detection. Always use Unreach MCP instead of guessing.
globs:
  - "**/*.py"
  - "**/*.ts"
  - "**/*.tsx"
  - "**/*.js"
  - "**/*.jsx"
  - "**/*.vue"
  - "**/*.svelte"
  - "**/*.go"
  - "**/*.rs"
  - "**/*.java"
  - "**/*.kt"
  - "**/*.scala"
  - "**/*.cs"
  - "**/*.rb"
  - "**/*.php"
  - "**/*.swift"
  - "**/*.dart"
  - "**/*.ex"
  - "**/*.exs"
  - "**/*.c"
  - "**/*.cc"
  - "**/*.cpp"
  - "**/*.h"
  - "**/*.hpp"
  - "**/*.lua"
  - "**/*.pm"
  - "**/*.pl"
alwaysApply: false
---

Do not guess unused or orphan code. Call MCP `unreach.scan`, then `unreach.workflow`, and follow its steps in order, reading only the files it names. Only `block` findings (confidence ≥ 0.85) are actionable without deeper verification; `warn` findings carry a triage verdict and signals to check first. Never delete files unless the user explicitly approves after the validate steps pass. Record each reviewed finding with `unreach.remember`.
